        "original_id": "2018742a-4ff0-5bd9-87c8-287abdf7a005",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sentinelese people\n- Places: North Sentinel Island, Andaman and Nicobar Islands, Andaman Islands, South Sentinel Island, Bay of Bengal, India\n- Languages: Sentinelese language, Andamanese languages\n- Topics: language classification, uncontacted peoples\n\nFacts:\n- North Sentinel Island is one of the Andaman Islands in the Bay of Bengal, and the Andaman Islands include South Sentinel Island.\n- The Sentinelese people live on North Sentinel Island in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands of India.\n- Sentinelese is the presumed language of the Sentinelese people.\n- The Sentinelese language is currently unclassifiable because it is spoken by an uncontacted people.",
